WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.200
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:10.820
That number is two one nine two David P. here's
a very important question about non voters

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.650
non-voters take a listen to this.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.610
Hey David.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:24.550
I was wondering with all the democratic candidates
outright now if your personal candidate doesn't

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:31.920
get picked, is there a certain number of people
that will just refuse to vote for the Democrats

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.920
because their candidate isn't the nominee
or is everyone just going to vote for the

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.920
Democrat?

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:34.920
Does that hurt?

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:41.430
There was a lot of issues last year where
there were a lot of people who were Bernie

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:48.200
supporters who were smirk that you didn't
get abomination and decided not to vote for

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.200
Hillary Clinton.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.360
So listen, I don't know the answer to that,
but it's something I am afraid of and we,

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.340
it is so important right now that we take
step one in starting to repair this country

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.680
and it is only step one, which is the removal
of Donald Trump.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:09.250
Earlier on today's program and on other programs,
I've talked extensively about the damage done

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.049
by Trump will extend far beyond his presidency.

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:16.990
The Republican party isn't fixed when Trump
leaves because the Republican party is what

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.070
allowed from to become their nominee and ultimately
to become the president.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:25.960
So when Trump leaves the Republican party,
it's still an absolutely abortive attempt

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.149
at being a reasonable political party.

00:01:28.149 --> 00:01:36.119
So we need to remove Trump is step one and
unfortunately it is conceivable that if someone

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:41.149
really likes one candidate and that candidate
is not the nominee, that some of them will

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:44.060
stay home or some might vote for Trump.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:47.789
Although I hope it's a very small number as
close to zero as possible.

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:50.590
Some may go third party, some may write in.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.450
I think that that's extremely problematic.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:59.709
Now if, if you're in a truly safe state, I
understand that your calculation may be different.

00:01:59.709 --> 00:02:03.909
Strictly speaking, I think that the right
way to approach this is assume the election

00:02:03.909 --> 00:02:06.520
could be close no matter where you're voting.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:11.769
I get that in Massachusetts, the Democrat
is going to defeat Donald Trump, and so if

00:02:11.769 --> 00:02:16.290
I vote third party or write someone in or
don't vote, it's not going to make a difference.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:21.840
But the problem with that logic is if everyone
who has that thought occur to them takes the

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.400
action, that does change things.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.959
So I think it's logically fallacious to fall
into that lack of thinking.

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:33.550
We should all just vote as if the election
did depend on our vote in terms of whether

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:37.319
people might just stay home because their
candidate isn't there.

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:45.189
My hope is that people who don't like Donald
Trump would realize that any of the democratic

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:49.040
options right now is better than Trump and
that thus they would vote.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:55.250
So I could understand people who are in the
Bernie Warren wing, if Joe Biden is the nominee

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.690
saying, I'm not voting for Biden.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:02.750
Biden says, we covered today that a, you know,
marijuana is a gateway drug.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:06.580
Biden's not for serious reform to the health
insurance system.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.120
I'm not going to vote for him what Trump is
worse.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.750
And I think at this point we have seen that
the let Trump win to break it all down and

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.030
then we'll rebuild it mentality.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.469
I mean, it just hasn't worked.

00:03:17.469 --> 00:03:19.060
It did, it didn't play out.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.409
It's not surprising that it didn't play out
that way.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:23.000
I think that is very dangerous thinking.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.170
So we'll have time to talk more about this.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:33.739
I do believe that we need to start seriously,
uh, talking about the reality that everybody

00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:38.180
should participate if turnout favors them.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.670
They win easily.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:44.170
Even with low Trump approval because of the
electoral college system that we have, particularly

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:49.540
if our sides turn out as depressed in those
key swing and battleground States.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.459
So I am very worried about it.

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:56.129
I don't want to be hyperbolic or alarmist,
but mathematically in those States where it's

00:03:56.129 --> 00:04:00.819
close, uh, some Democrats saying, I'm not
voting because my guy or gal is not.

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:04.099
The nominee could turn some States for Trump.

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:05.459
And it could turn the election for Trump.

00:04:05.459 --> 00:04:07.420
We don't want to let that happen and we'll
talk about it more.

